        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Moorea is an outstanding detached family home of distinctive architectural style, situated on secluded private landscaped gardens of approximately 1 acre with a private tennis court on a quiet residential road in the heart of Foxrock, one of Dublin’s most sought-after and prestigious suburbs.\r\nThis distinguished and unique home is approached to the front through impressive wrought iron vehicular entrance gates flanked by extensive mature high hedging which allude to the privacy and seclusion beyond. Despite the striking and attractive façade, it is not possible to appreciate the extraordinarily generous and elegant accommodation within from an exterior glance. Presented in excellent order and tastefully appointed throughout, Moorea boasts light filled interiors extending to 373sq.m /4,014sq.ft and enjoys dual aspect views over the gardens from numerous rooms.\r\nInternally, the expansive family accommodation is laid out over two floors.  An entrance hall leads to a spectacular double height, inner reception hall which is a wonderful surprise and immediately sets the tone for this magnificent home.\r\nAt ground floor, there is very elegant yet comfortable family living accommodation to include, a drawing room/dining rooms with a feature high ceiling, a majestic fireplace and expansive views over the front and rear gardens. which leads into a conservatory with access to a private garden to the front of the house. The dining area connects to the kitchen, affording seamless catering for family gatherings.  A calm, elegant family room presents a serene space for reading and enjoys a front aspect. There is a beautifully appointed solid oak Dalkey Design kitchen at the heart of the house with bespoke cabinetry and complete with Aga adding to the warmth of this special family home. There is also a spacious utility room and guest w.c. with access to the terrace area. To the rear of the house there is a well-appointed and comfortable study. There is a guest bedroom complemented by an ensuite, and two double bedrooms and a bathroom, completing the accommodation at this level.\r\nA truly elegant mahogany staircase with a distinctive curve gently leads you from the ground floor to the upper floor.\r\nAt first floor the main suite presents a spacious bedroom with bespoke cabinetry, complemented by two dressing rooms, and a luxurious bathroom. There is one further ensuite bedroom, a playroom and luggage room providing an abundance of storage. This is a wonderful ‘get away’ space which enjoys privacy and seclusion from the rest of the house, ideal for teenagers or for visitor accommodation, it is an additional bonus to the already extensive accommodation below.\r\nMoorea sits comfortably within its own grounds of cleverly designed landscaped gardens offering a variety of options from which to enjoy the private grounds. To the front there is a secluded private garden which benefits from westerly sunshine, generous off-street garden and a variety of specimen trees and shrubs. The dual side access leads you to the delightful rear gardens with rolling lawns, and a generous terrace, ideal for summer gatherings, whilst overlooking the pond, or playing a game of tennis. The pavilion is a very comfortable seating area, providing a view over the gardens with an array of specimen trees, shrubs, and herbaceous borders. The storeroom has been adapted to a games room, complete with table tennis and activity area. The landscaped gardens surround the property and provide ample outdoor space accessed from several areas within the house. \r\n\r\nThe location of Moorea is second to none with Foxrock and Cabinteely villages on its doorstep, providing an array of amenities, including a choice of bijou shops, eateries, supermarkets, independent stores and services. Leopardstown Racecourse and Golf Centre is also nearby. Foxrock Golf Club, Carrickmines Golf Club and Carrickmines Lawn Tennis & Croquet Club are within very easy reach. Woodland walks, playground, sports playing fields and coffee shops can all be found at the nearby Cabinteely Park. \r\n\r\nSome of Dublin’s finest primary and secondary schools are within easy reach including St Brigid’s and Hollypark national schools, Loreto College Foxrock, Mount Anville, St Andrews College, Clonkeen College, Willow Park and Blackrock College, Colaiste Eoin and Iosagain.  University College Dublin and Trinity College are easily accessible by public transport. Excellent transport links are close by including the QBC, N11, M50 and the LUAS providing ease of access to and from the city centre and surrounding areas."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "ENTRANCE PORCH\r\n3.78m x 2.15m (12'4\" x 7'0\")\r\nPicture light, recessed lighting and quarry tiled floor. Door with leaded stained-glass detail to:\r\n\r\nRECEPTION HALL\r\n4.85m x 3.95m (15'10\" x 12'11\")\r\nDecorative wall panelling and radiator cover. Picture light, recessed lighting and stripped and polished wooden floor. Cloaks cupboard.\r\n\r\nGUEST WC\r\nWhite suite incorporating a pedestal wash hand basin and wc. Recessed lighting and stripped and polished wooden floor.\r\n\r\nDRAWING / DINING ROOM\r\n8.43m x 7.6m (27'7\" x 24'11\")\r\nMajestic Adam’s Style marble fireplace with marble inset brass surround and marble hearth. Dual aspect room with a feature vaulted ceiling. Patio doors to the terrace and gardens.\r\n\r\nFAMILY ROOM\r\n4.38m x 4.0m (14'4\" x 13'1\")\r\nFeature marble fireplace with cast iron inset and a marble hearth incorporating a coal effect gas fire, flanked by a library and entertainment unit. Decorative ceiling coving and recessed lighting. View over the gardens.\r\n\r\nKITCHEN/BREAKFAST/LIVING ROOM\r\n\r\nKITCHEN AREA\r\n3.91m x 3.52m (12'9\" x 11'6\")\r\nSuperb range of hand painted solid wood fitted units incorporating illuminated quartz worktop areas with quartz surround. Quality appliances to include a Neff double oven and four ring gas hob, an integrated Siemens dishwasher, an integrated Liebherr fridge/freezer and a two door Aga. Recessed lighting and stripped and polished wooden floor. Feature island unit with a quartz top incorporating a stainless-steel unit.\r\n\r\nBREAKFAST/LIVING AREA\r\n6.5m x 5.32m (21'3\" x 17'5\")\r\nFeature vaulted ceiling and picture windows overlooking the gardens. Cherrywood fireplace with cast iron inset incorporating a coal effect gas fire. Decorative radiator covers and stripped and polished wooden floor. Door to the gardens.\r\n\r\nUTILITY ROOM\r\n3.25m x 2.5m\r\nRange of fitted units providing generous storage for coats and cloaks. Fitted Miele washing machine and Bosch dryer. Tiled floor and recessed lighting. Door to garden. Gardeners cloak room.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 1\r\n4.4m x 3.0m (14'5\" x 9'10\")\r\nDouble fitted wardrobes and vanity unit with mirror detail.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 2\r\n4.25m x 3.2m (13'11\" x 10'5\")\r\nDouble built in wardrobes. Triple aspect room with French doors to the gardens.\r\n\r\nENSUITE\r\nWhite suite incorporating a shower unit, pedestal wash hand basin, wall lighting and wc. Tiled walls and floor and recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nWALK IN LINEN CUPBOARD\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 3\r\n4.14m x 2.8m (13'6\" x 9'2\")\r\nFloor to ceiling fitted wardrobes with shelving detail.\r\n\r\nBATHROOM\r\n2.76m x 2.23m (9'0\" x 7'3\")\r\nWhite suite incorporating a bath with telephone shower attachment, shower unit, wall lighting, pedestal wash hand basin and wc. Tiled walls and floor and recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nSTUDY\r\n4.0m x 3.42m (13'1\" x 11'2\")\r\nBespoke library and desk with filing storage and shelving. Feature vaulted ceiling and French doors to the gardens.\r\n\r\nSTAIRCASE TO THE FIRST FLOOR\r\n\r\nMAIN SUITE\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 4\r\n5.41m x 3.38m (17'8\" x 11'1\")\r\nHand crafted wardrobes presses, chest of drawers, library shelving and window seat.\r\n\r\nDRESSING ROOM 1\r\n3.06m x 3.14m (10'0\" x 10'3\")\r\nHand crafted wardrobe and panelling detail.\r\n\r\nDRESSING ROOM 2\r\n3.4m x 3.22m (11'1\" x 10'6\")\r\nBespoke fitted wardrobes and vanity unit.\r\n\r\nBATHROOM\r\nDuravit white suite incorporating a free-standing bath, a fully tiled shower unit, a wash hand basin perched on a marble top, heated towel rail and wc. Porcelain tiled floor, panelling detail, recessed lighting and under floor heating.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 5\r\n4.14m x 2.97m (13'6\" x 9'8\")\r\nFeature window seat, port hole window and panelling detail.\r\n\r\nENSUITE\r\nWhite suite incorporating a fully tiled shower unit, pedestal wash hand basin, heated towel rail, wall light and wc. Tiled walls and floor.\r\n\r\nPLAYROOM\r\nAccess to under eaves storage. This is a non-habitable space and is not included in the overall size. Door to luggage storage."
      },
